"# My day\nA little long, so let’s see how much I can piece together after the fact\\.\n- I get in at 8:30\\.\n- Some chatting with Will about when to meet about things, some revision of email because Dr. Terror wants to reschedule and Tomer isn’t on the project\n- End up chatting one on one with Will\n- Takeaway is, there isn’t much to do, though we can find stuff, but the hours are super flexible, so that’s where I can take my 20 Civic Time hours out of primarily\\.\n- The environment seems like a secondary priority, the way he kind of swerved away from it\n- The whole thing is just weird\n- Anyway, actual pressing issue was that he was having issues recording multiple videos in a single play run\n\t- When I recreated it, it would do one video fine, but then subsequent ones would throw a memory error and result in a blank, black video with full audio\n- And I dug into that and, I think, solved it by disabling “GPU Encoding”, which stopped a memory error from happening, which resulted in no recording problems\n- Reported back to him, merged it in, and he said actually he wasn’t having the issue today\\. So who knows?\n- \\(Also, between chatting with Will and fixing the issue, I disappeared for 30 minutes to Newbury\\)\n\t- Picked up “Monica Rambeau: Photon”, first issue of a new miniseries\n\t- Didn’t pick up another “Lovecraft: Unknown Kadath” thing because I gotta stop\n\t- Looked over the clearance stuff and stumbled across a big hardcover UmbrEdgar Academy Vol\\. 2 “Dallas” for $20, and impulse bought as a Christmas gift for Lincoln\\.\n- \\(Also also, lunch was in here somewhere\\)\n- At this point, it’s time for a meetup for KR where me, Toronto, Miguel and Frodo debrief from yesterday and make a plan\n- There’s still stuff Miguel wants to interrogate Dimestore and Bobby about regarding our final plans\n- I tried cleaning up the graph/network/thing Dimestore had set up showing how all of our things connected, in order to get rid of criss\\-crossing lines and loops and stuff, and get an actual graph with flow to it\n\t- And what came from that was a potentially perfect answer to a question we had\\.\n\t- We were trying to figure out how to get ATO mission estimated end times to Frodo, who needed to do something with them\n\t- What that meant was getting them into the Rules Engine\n\t- Meaning the Map Tool, which handles the ATOs, is connected to both \\[INTERNALLY USED SIM NAME\\] and the rules engine\n\t- And it means that the map tool just creates arbitrary Datums for each end \\(and start\\) time which, while functional, is ugly\n\t- But, in disentangling the overall distributed system plan, and in seeing what happens if we only connect the map to \\[INTERNALLY USED SIM NAME\\], the answer became clear\n\t\t- When creating platforms, allow for AUX\\_DATA keys and values to be given to the platform, and then spit those out in platform metrics\n\t\t- That way, we can give start and end times to the AUX\\_DATA, have it internally in \\[INTERNALLY USED SIM NAME\\] with the platform, and have them be something Frodo can read and make use of cleanly instead of relying on arbitrary rules\\.\n\t\t- And this can be super useful in the future for any number of use cases\n\t\t- And all of this in an overall system with actual flow, instead of lines criss\\-crossing and everything touching everything\n- So we get out of this meeting, and then there’s italian food left over in M building, and then we go there and there’s nothing there of interest to me except bread and cookies \\(there’s lasagna, a meatball or two, the leftovers of, I guess, chicken and pasta alfredo\\.\\.\\. nothing to write home about\\. Was hoping for Chateau\\.\\)\n- We come back and Bobby is ready to do scanning stuff\n\t- I had shot him a message this morning asking to schedule some time today to scan him\\.\n\t- And he was ready early, and I ended up just putting 2 hours towards the Civic Time 3D scanning goals\\.\n- So first, I scanned Bobby’s head with Heges\\.\n\t- First scan was mostly okay, and is probably the best, but there’s stray floating geometry\n\t\t- Also the backs of the ears don’t work well, because they’re thin enough that it can’t figure them out\n\n![](dayone-moment://F78795E936CF42C890B20214A580ED09)\n\n![](dayone-moment://6FE547630952479B80349ADF1449E3CD)\n\n\t- Second scan, eyes closed, was worse\n\t- Bobby figured out that the floating nose bit was probably the result of starting on the left side, then going around the back to get the full head scan, then doing the face at the end\n\t\t- I think the takeaway might be that I need to do a really good face shot and a really good full head thing, and put them together in post\n\n![](dayone-moment://48C8D25E42944BDAA9E7E1BD5341CBB1)\n\n- Then we tried a body scan with Polycam\n\n![](dayone-moment://A13339B1DE0C48C1BF4FA48DA14307F7)\n\n\t- Face was a mess, hands were a mess, rest was\\.\\.\\. a little less of a mess\\. \n\t- The rest was imperfect, but workable\\. Clear enough that it’s pants and a shirt, even if the textures could maybe use some adjusting to fix the seams\n- Then we tried hand scanning\n\t- Tried a couple different ways \\- him holding hands out in a couple positions, etc\\.\n\n![](dayone-moment://5061DDAC90AC4EF1B732C19EC1A453F7)\n\n![](dayone-moment://8EA90614AB9A4F7CA561B126A1134F1F)\n\n\t- Finally just went over to a table and scanned each side separately\\. We’ll see if we can stitch those together\n\n![](dayone-moment://CA43E301B9E143EA94E58B3096DA242D)\n\n![](dayone-moment://248C3939B20D42FE9A9AAFD8DBF71B9F)\n\n\t- Original plan had been to scan both hands, but I was tired of that cannoli after a couple scans so we just did one\n\t- Part of the issue is that it loses tracking when crossing over the edge of the hand \\- not enough detail\n\t- I have enough partial scans though that maybe I can make use of some of them for the arms\\. Dunno\\.\n- Oh cannoli I forgot to get some good photos of his glasses\\. And maybe his eyes\\.\n- I had a couple random thoughts after the fact\n\t- Tried the “take photos and send em to be photogrammetried on the cloud” approach to a hand\\.\n\t\t- It went terribly\n\n![](dayone-moment://38E1272784AF4198AE68560C61E7F8B3)\n\n\t- This morning I realized I could scan myself by moving my head instead of the phone\n\t\t- And it went well for me\n\n![](dayone-moment://8670A1CDD4114DE485265DA4DD75637C)\n\n\t\t- So I tried it with Bobby\n\t\t- It didn’t work well for him\\. We tried twice\\.\n\n![](dayone-moment://709E2A0F61BF402189569DFD4CB365C4)\n\n![](dayone-moment://AE945A21AAB342D5B69BB38720725789)\n\n- Bobby left, perhaps to go down to the other area he works now\n- I did a quick scan of the lab\n\n![](dayone-moment://B9C04F004AEF4440B07E50AC1B476AF5)\n\n- I put the body scan of Bobby in the scan of the lab in Blender\n\t- Sent him a pic of that, along with the 3D models just in case he had any interest in playing with them\n- Then it was 5:00 and D&D time\n\t- While we were waiting, I scanned the room we were in for fun\n\n![](dayone-moment://45D2FBBC8C1B4B6CBD563710A4FC02FC)\n\n- Started with me and Toronto disguised as vampires in a rich lady’s house trying to steal back some stolen bones\\. Toronto figured out how to get her to show us the bones \\(“we gotta count them to make sure”\\), and I figured out how to steal them \\(use an illusion to make it look like they’re still there\\)\n- Jordan was there for the first half, but left, leaving just me, Toronto and Rob\\.\n- Then we reconsecrated the church, were brought out into the town’s mandatory festival, where Dracula showed up, and then a riot started, and then we went back to the church which we thought we’d consecrated but it’s unclear if that stopped Dracula \\(“Strahd von Zarovitch”, technically\\.\\)\n\t- I wanted to kill the burgomaster with fire and oil but I didn’t get the chance\n- We came back to the church to protect Irina, who Dracula was after and who we thought was safe\n\t- Doors open, priest dead, large figure inside\n\t- We thought “oh, I bet that’s that big strong guy, I’ll disguise myself as Dracula and the other two will go invisible and we’ll sneak by this guy and go upstairs and see what’s what”\n- So we do that, go in, and we were dead wrong, because it’s actually 3 giant direwolves and also some swarms of bats\n- It’s immediately clear we are in over our heads and what follows is a long drawn out “fight” sequence in which we are bolting for the stairs on the opposite end of the church, where the Direwolves may not be able to go\n\t- Just a mad dash through monsters towards the exit\n\t- Two of us made it, but the session ended before Rob made it all the way\\. He kept falling and being attacked, so it’s good that he’s also the “tank”, with the most health and damage resistance\n\t- I almost died\\. I’m very low on health and we don’t know what’s waiting for us\n\t- I was keeping Rob invisible and that stopped working pretty quickly\n\t- Toronto managed to keep herself invisible the whole time and took no\\(?\\) damage\n- It was all very dramatic, and we won’t know what awaits us upstairs until next session, which will probably be 4 weeks from now because of the holidays, and also Toronto will be out of the country\n- On our way out, we think we saw Frodo with a  group of people in another conference room, but the windows were\\.\\.\\. what’s the word for when it looks fogged but it’s intentional\\.\\.\\. anyway, I think she waved, I’m pretty sure it was her, I don’t know if it was a D&D session in a different room on a different night or not \\(our understanding was she does it thursdays in the Frodoe room we use\\)\n- Came home\\. Parents are out\\. Made mac and cheese for dinner\\. Cabot is so much more flavorful than Annies\\.\n- And now here I am, typing this up\\. Need to get some screenshots of my scans to add to this entry\\.\n- Mortimer said good night while I was in the D&D session and I did the\\.\\.\\. right? thing and just said “night”\n- And I think that covers it\\.\n\n---\n\nUpdate from morning after: “Frosted”\\. “Frosted glass”\\. I think\\. Now that I’ve said it, I might be wrong\\."
